hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27545","Yunus ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said: Hammad, meaning Ibn Salamah, narrated to us, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Qasim, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Sahlah, wife of Abu Hudhayfah, that she said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, Salim, the freedman of Abu Hudhayfah, enters upon me while he is bearded. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Suckle him. She said: How shall I suckle him while he is bearded? So she suckled him, and he used to enter upon her."
